# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — 2026-10-22 02:50:23 UTC

Base revision: `a526dea9`. This entry records the request 201
`getAllSubscriptionGroup` protocol and RPC slice. Pinned Java source is
`efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.

## Compatibility changes

- Added Java-compatible `GetAllSubscriptionGroupRequestHeader` and response
  total header, including nullable fields and public accessor inventory.
- Added `SubscriptionGroupWrapper` with Java constructor defaults, nullable
  tables, `DataVersion`, subscription-group configs, and forbidden-topic map.
- Added `MQClientApi::get_all_subscription_group` for request 201. It applies
  configured VIP routing and metadata page size, shares one overall deadline,
  aggregates both tables, restarts and clears both on version changes, and
  treats missing/invalid `totalGroupNum` as a complete legacy-Broker response.
- Added Java invocation cases for one/multiple pages, version restart, legacy
  response, Broker failure, missing/null/malformed bodies, invalid total, and
  timeout after a page. The version-restart case proves stale group and
  forbidden rows are removed together.
- Added bidirectional typed-header/body fixtures and updated the direct API
  reverse-audit count from 11 open operations to 10.

## Local verification

- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --locked`: passed.
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-core --test admin_rpc --locked`: 96 passed.
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-core --lib --locked`: 199 passed.
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-protocol -p rocketmq-classic-core --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check`: passed.
- `mvn -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`: BUILD SUCCESS; includes
  Java fixture verification, all 95 Rust typed-header cross-decodes and all 18
  Rust typed-body cross-decodes.
- Producer core and query-admin header fixture verification passed.
- SHA-256 `fixtures/producer/core.json`:
  `c6b0fea6eca62451184b31ef87bb37ce358d07bcb9acea20a9bb9d9f86e3689b`.
- SHA-256 `fixtures/remoting/query-admin-header-decode-modes.json`:
  `ca1aa14c902ee60b69a4abca48679bc79af00bfa0c5badd24532e53518a8e6e4`.

One initial compatibility test used Java's zero-timeout proxy with an empty
reply queue, so the oracle emitted `NoSuchElementException` before exercising
the timeout behavior. That mock-only case was removed; the real timeout-after-
page case remains in both Java and Rust tests and passes.

## Remaining work

The request 201 slice is closed. The pinned `MQClientAPIImpl` direct-operation
reverse audit still has 10 open rows, and the wider Phase 18 settings, inputs,
errors, control flows, reverse-export audit, and platform evidence remain
open. No Broker, Docker, or remote CI was used. Pre-existing Phase 19 worktree
paths remain unstaged and outside this slice.
